### Mock hospital scheduling API (Lab 3) – synthetic data only
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" / IntelliJ HTTP client. The JSON files next to this file are
### real request/response pairs captured from the running application.

@base = http://localhost:8083
@camunda = http://localhost:8080/v2

### 1. Register an availability request (done by job worker triage.request-availability)
POST {{base}}/mock/scheduling/availability-requests
Content-Type: application/json

< ./01-register-availability-request.request.json

### 2. Free slots at the main hospital (REST Connector "Retrieve available slots")
GET {{base}}/mock/scheduling/availability-requests/AR-XXXXXXXX/slots?site=MAIN_HOSPITAL
Accept: application/json

### 3. Free slots at the partner clinic (REST Connector "Search partner clinic") - see 08/09 for NEUROLOGY
GET {{base}}/mock/scheduling/availability-requests/AR-XXXXXXXX/slots?site=PARTNER_CLINIC
Accept: application/json

### 4. Book a slot (job worker triage.book-appointment); a slot that is already taken answers HTTP 409 (see 11)
POST {{base}}/mock/scheduling/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

< ./03-book-slot.request.json

### 5. Release an unconfirmed booking (job worker triage.release-slot)
POST {{base}}/mock/scheduling/bookings/BK-XXXXXXXX/cancellation

### 6. Fault injection: list / break / repair
GET {{base}}/admin/faults

###
POST {{base}}/admin/faults/scheduling-api-down?enabled=true

###
POST {{base}}/admin/faults/scheduling-api-down?enabled=false

### "Another patient" takes every slot we try to book until the next slot query (re-query demo)
POST {{base}}/admin/faults/booking-conflict-once?enabled=true

### 7. Start a process instance (Camunda 8 Run Orchestration Cluster API, unprotected locally)
POST {{camunda}}/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "processDefinitionId": "patient-appointment-triage",
  "variables": {
    "patientReference": "SYN-P-0201",
    "patientAge": 34,
    "appointmentPreference": {"department": "GENERAL_PRACTICE", "preferredDate": "2026-11-03", "timeOfDay": "MORNING"},
    "symptomsSummary": "Mild cough and sore throat for a few days",
    "painLevel": 2,
    "symptomDurationDays": 3
  }
}

### 8. The patient confirms the appointment (message correlated by patientReference)
POST {{camunda}}/messages/publication
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "appointment-confirmed",
  "correlationKey": "SYN-P-0201",
  "variables": {"confirmedVia": "SMS reply (synthetic)"}
}

### 9. Evaluate the triage decision on its own
POST {{camunda}}/decision-definitions/evaluation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decisionDefinitionId": "triage-category",
  "variables": {"chestPain": false, "breathingDifficulty": false, "painLevel": 6, "highFever": false,
                "patientAge": 52, "symptomDurationDays": 10}
}
